MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-07 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: - Managing a command information program designed to keep assigned staff members, (e.g., military staff and civilian employees), informed of organizational, (e.g., Navy), significant national/international events and policy decisions;
- Meeting with organizational councils and committees to deal with morale, human relations and other people-related issues, providing advice on methods of communicating presenting and approach to the internal publicity;
- Serving as focal point of contact in the organization',(e.g., NHB ), Public Affairs office for inquiries received from reporters, writers, producers and editors of national and international news media;
- Advocating for patients, incumbent facilities resolution of problems and/or initiates patient concerns through department of division concerned, providing solutions to inquiries in a timely manner.
- Coordinating with the Command Privacy Officer for the protection of patient privacy and compliance with Health Insurance Portability and Accountability (HIPAA). Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=GS-ADMIN https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/1000/public-affairs-series-1035/
